    still select it.
  - [38;5;153mREADME.md[39m says production has [1m48,000 rows[0m in [38;5;153musers[39m, and migrations are applied in order automatically by the deploy
    job. So merging this is the same action as deleting that column's production data — there's no separate "apply it
    later when we're ready" step.
  - [38;5;153mALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN notes[39m is irreversible. A rollback migration can recreate an empty [38;5;153mnotes[39m column, not
    its contents. Once it runs, whatever text is in those 48,000 rows is gone unless a database backup or export exists.

